# Build context for BOTH root-context images: the service (`docker build .`)
# and tripl-mcp (`docker build -f mcp-server/Dockerfile .`, which moved to the
# root context so it can reach ./cli — tripl-ey6j.1). Keep this tight: the
# multi-arch release builds send the context to the builder, so excluding VCS,
# deps, caches, and secrets makes builds faster and avoids leaking .env.
#
# NOTE: the Dockerfiles copy backend/src, backend/alembic*, the whole frontend/
# tree, and cli/ + mcp-server/src — do NOT ignore those. We only drop deps,
# caches, and outputs that the images rebuild themselves (node_modules, .venv,
# dist). In particular `*.md` below is a ROOT-LEVEL pattern (`*` does not match
# `/`), so cli/README.md and mcp-server/README.md still ship — both are declared
# as `readme` in their pyproject and `uv sync` fails without them.

# VCS
.git/
.gitattributes

# Python caches / virtualenvs (image runs `uv sync` itself)
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Built Python artifacts (`uv build` output, never installed from in-image)
cli/dist/
mcp-server/dist/

# Node (image runs `bun install` + `bun run build` itself)
**/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
**/.vite/
**/coverage/

# Local env / secrets — never send these to the builder
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime/user data
var/
**/var/

# Tooling, agents, and docs not needed to build the image
.github/
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/
.ecc/
.serena/
.aws/
.omc/
.beads/
.design-sync/
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/
design/
docs/
internal/
graphify-out/
assets/

# Compose, helper scripts, and markdown (not copied into the image)
compose*.yaml
bin/
*.md
PLAN.md
skills-lock.json

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
